cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it as below, and cite the original data sources separately."
title: "MYC-paralog regulatory hubs in small cell lung cancer"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible multi-omics analysis that translates paralog-resolved MYC,
  MYCN and MYCL1 regulatory programs from small cell lung cancer cell lines
  into patient tumours, and applies a weight-free, two-stage rank-aggregation
  framework to combine independent evidence layers. Regulons are anchored on
  measured paralog binding rather than motif inference, because all three
  paralogs share the canonical E-box and motif-based methods cannot
  distinguish them. The two principal findings are negative and were
  registered as reportable before any result existed: paralog identity does
  not survive in patient tumours, where neuroendocrine lineage state accounts
  for regulon activity, and the integration framework returns no ranked hub
  list, its two surviving evidence domains converging in aggregate but not at
  the level of individual genes.
type: software
